{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xiii", "label": "Article XIII \u2014 Corrections do not erase history", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-20-sections.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_xviii", "label": "Article XVIII \u2014 Political neutrality is structural", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-20-sections.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_06_api_and_ui_s6", "label": "06 \u00a76 \u2014 Counts by state, no ranking, no score for a speaker", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-20-sections.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_20_sections_stage", "label": "Stage 20 \u2014 Sections and placements in the log (implemented)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-20-sections.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sections are organizational rather than epistemic, but they are shared structure many principals add to over weeks and the public reads a speech through them, so filing must be attributed, replayable and reversible. Stage 15's TAG_CLAIM set the precedent. Two alternatives were rejected: sections as SOURCE_LOCATION rows (a subject is not one range of a recording) and a tree outside the log (a volunteer's placement arrives inside a signed TASK_RESULT and would have nowhere signed to land)."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_20_sections_create_section", "label": "CREATE_SECTION \u2014 one contribution creates one subtree", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-20-sections.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An assistant records an outline of a few hundred sections in one signed write: nested at most 6 levels, 500 nodes per contribution, 2,000 per root, 120-character headings, and a 300-character quoted anchor that locates the place rather than reproducing the passage. Headings are untrusted display text, never scored. Ids derive from the contribution in preorder."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_20_sections_place_claim", "label": "PLACE_CLAIM \u2014 filing is not certifying", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-20-sections.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Accepted on validation for any principal, because a placement changes no score and is reversible by INVALIDATE, so Article XI is untouched. A claim born in a section is one contribution; inside a TASK_RESULT the placement counts only when the result does."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_20_sections_no_score_for_a_section", "label": "No probability, headline or badge for a section, source or speaker", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-20-sections.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A speech is never given a score, only counts by assessment state rolled up from children, and the fixed note \"counts depend on extraction granularity\" travels with every rendering and JSON. Investigations::Verdict and Cards::StatementImage refuse a section; a root's share card is its counts."}], "edges": [{"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_20_sections_stage", "target": "implementation_implem